UNITED STATES MISSION TO THE UNITED NATIONS
Office of Press and Public Diplomacy
FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE
U.S. Mission Hosts Event in Support of ITU Secretary-General Candidate Doreen Bogdan-Martin
The below is attributable to a U.S. Mission to the United Nations spokesperson:
The U.S. Representative of the United States to the Economic and Social Council of the United Nations, Ambassador Dan Negrea, hosted on Tuesday, December 16th, a roundtable discussion with U.S. private sector leaders and Ms. Doreen Bogdan-Martin, the U.S. candidate for re-election as Secretary-General of the International Telecommunication Union (ITU) for the 2027 to 2030 term.
Representatives from Amazon, Google, Mastercard, Meta, Microsoft, Salesforce, and the U.S. Council for International Business joined the discussion.
The session was focused on the importance of the ITU to U.S. industry and how continued U.S. leadership can strengthen global digital connectivity and advance core economic and security interests. Participants were able to exchange views with Ms. Bogdan-Martin on the future of international telecommunications policy and the role of the ITU in supporting innovation and open, secure, and reliable networks.
The United States is also running for a seat on the ITU Council as well as supporting Ms. Jennifer Warren for the Radio Regulations Board at the ITU. Continued U.S. leadership at the ITU helps ensure all can benefit from a stable and trustworthy digital environment.
