Ambassador Jennifer Locetta
Alternative Representative for Special Political Affairs
New York, New York
AS DELIVERED
Thank you. The United States extends its appreciation to Guyana, who has diligently led the UN Haiti sanctions committee while on the Council. We appreciate their efforts as chair of the committee to further peace and stability in Haiti.
The United States also appreciates the Panel of Experts’ efforts to provide detailed reporting and analysis on Haiti’s security, political, and humanitarian crisis, informing international efforts to address gang violence and support stability.
We remain seized with the crisis in Haiti, especially the expansion of terrorist gang control. Viv Ansanm and Gran Grif’s growing violence must be stopped.
We applaud the Council’s decisive action in the most recent Haiti sanctions renewal to designate Kempes Sanon and Dimitri Herard. These individuals played a significant role in bolstering the criminal networks and gangs in Haiti.
Nevertheless, the United States calls for sanctions against additional enablers of insecurity. We call on our colleagues on this Council to provide full and unqualified support to these designations as we move forward.
Finally, the United States welcomes the Council’s urging for annual reporting from the Haitian authorities on the implementation of the sanctions regime to further promote accountability.
The United States remains committed to working with Haiti, regional partners, and the international community to facilitate peace, security, and prosperity for Haiti’s future.
Thank you.
