EOV on a GA Resolution on Strengthening of international cooperation and coordination of efforts to study, mitigate and minimize the consequences of the Chornobyl disaster
Katherine Ring
Foreign Affairs Officer
New York, New York
AS PREPARED
The United States thanks Ukraine for putting forward its resolution on Strengthening of international cooperation and coordination of efforts to study, mitigate and minimize the consequences of the Chornobyl disaster.
The United States voted against this text because of references to the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development and related language. The 2030 Agenda and the Sustainable Development Goals advance a program of soft global governance inconsistent with national sovereignty and adverse to U.S. interests.
The United States continues to reiterate its commitment and support for international nuclear safety and security standards and guidance for nuclear facilities, and supports the continued efforts to prevent a nuclear incident at Ukraine’s nuclear facilities during the Russia-Ukraine war.
