Readout of Ambassador Mike Waltz’s Meeting with His Majesty King Abdullah II of Jordan
The below is attributable to a U.S. Mission to the United Nations spokesperson:
Ambassador Mike Waltz, Representative of the United States to the United Nations, met with His Majesty King Abdullah II of Jordan, on December 7, 2025, to discuss important bilateral and regional issues, especially the need to implement all parts of President Trump’s 20-point Comprehensive Plan to End the Gaza Conflict. The Ambassador thanked the King for all of Jordan’s efforts to bring humanitarian relief to Palestinians in Gaza, in line with the President’s plan. In addition, they discussed the need for stability in the West Bank. The Ambassador and the King discussed areas of bilateral cooperation and how to expand this partnership at the United Nations.
Ambassador Waltz emphasized continued U.S. support for peace, stability, and prosperity in the region in cooperation with the Hashemite Kingdom of Jordan.
