Readout of Ambassador Mike Waltz’s Meeting withIsraeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu
The below is attributable to a U.S. Mission to the United Nations spokesperson:
Ambassador Mike Waltz, Representative of the United States to the United Nations, met today with Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. Ambassador Waltz reaffirmed the United States’ commitment to Israel’s security and discussed ongoing efforts to maintain the Gaza ceasefire, release of the remaining hostage, and implementation of the U.S.-drafted UN Security Council Resolution 2803, which advances President Trump’s 20-Point Plan.
Ambassador Waltz welcomed Israel’s cooperation on expanding border crossings, including the Allenby-King Hussein Bridge crossing, for the delivery of humanitarian aid to Gaza and emphasized the importance of continued collaboration to address regional stability.
