Ambassador Jennifer Locetta
Alternative Representative for Special Political Affairs
New York, New York
AS DELIVERED
Thank you, Madam President, and thank you, Madam Minister, for your participation today.
We appreciate Finland’s principled leadership of the OSCE this year, the 50th Anniversary of the Helsinki Final Act. You and your teams in Vienna and Helsinki have worked hard to begin to position the OSCE to better respond to current and future challenges.
At this time, as the bloodiest war in recent history rages in Europe, organizations that support peace are important. Ending the Russia-Ukraine war is a top priority for President Trump. And it is time to build sustainable peace through negotiation. The killing must stop. We appreciate and welcome the OSCE’s readiness to play a supporting role in this process.
As President Trump made clear in his speech at the UN General Assembly, international organizations need to return to their core mandates, cut bloat, and modernize. This includes the OSCE.
Madam Minister, we commend the steps taken during your chairmanship to develop a reform agenda, including in discussions at the Ministerial meeting you hosted in Vienna.
The OSCE must return to its core mission of promoting peace, preventing wars, and increasing prosperity. Narrowing focus and scope logically means tighter resourcing. Fiscal reform and rightsizing of OSCE institutions and missions are important to maximizing effectiveness.
We believe OSCE reform is necessary to ensure the Organization can fulfill its mission of advancing security in Europe, and provide a venue where states with divergent visions of society can effectively meet, negotiate, and manage their differences.
We want to ensure that the OSCE of 2026 and beyond serves as a platform that enables participating States to work on pressing security issues. This includes conventional arms control and border security, and to counter threats like terrorism, money laundering, and trafficking. We need an OSCE that is ready to help secure a peace once President Trump succeeds in ending the war between Russia and Ukraine.
By continuing the longstanding collaboration between the OSCE and the UN, we can leverage our collective strength to address complex global challenges more effectively.
Thank you.
